IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il37-nouns`
IMPORT `il37-committee`

-- Tests for who sits on the committee and the majority for a decision (s 4(b) to (f)). Row IL-37.
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the text of the instrument (SH 3388 p. 434), never from the code's output.
-- A tally builder takes one BOOLEAN per seat, in this order of the committee from the 26th Knesset:
--   President, justice, justice, Minister of Justice, other minister, coalition Knesset member, opposition Knesset member,
--   public representative of the coalition, public representative of the opposition.
-- For the case of more than 80 the last two seats are the public representatives whom the Knesset as a whole chose (s 4(f)(2)).

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` MEANS
    LIST (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the President of the Supreme Court`, a),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, b),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, c),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Minister of Justice`, d),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another minister whom the Government names`, e),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`, f),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`, g),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose`, h),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose`, i)

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
`the nine under section 4(f) in order` MEANS
    LIST (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the President of the Supreme Court`, a),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, b),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, c),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Minister of Justice`, d),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another minister whom the Government names`, e),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`, f),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`, g),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose`, h),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose`, i)

`ordinary judge` MEANS `the election of a judge of a court other than the Supreme Court`
`supreme judge` MEANS `the election of a judge of the Supreme Court`
`other decision` MEANS `a decision that is not the election of a judge`

§ `The seats of each vintage`

#ASSERT count (`the seats of the committee` `the text before the 26th Knesset` FALSE) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count (`the seats of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` FALSE) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count (`the seats of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` TRUE) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count (`the seats of the committee` `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` FALSE) EQUALS 9
-- The old committee has the Bar's two seats; the new one has none and has the two public representatives instead.
#ASSERT elem `a representative of the Bar Association` (`the seats of the committee` `the text before the 26th Knesset` FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT elem `a representative of the Bar Association` (`the seats of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT elem `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose` (`the seats of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT elem `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose` (`the seats of the committee` `the text before the 26th Knesset` FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- With more than 80, the Knesset as a whole chooses both public representatives.
#ASSERT elem `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose` (`the seats of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT elem `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose` (`the seats of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the seat chairs the committee` `the Minister of Justice` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the seat chairs the committee` `another minister whom the Government names` EQUALS FALSE

§ `The paragraph of s 4(d) each seat is in`

#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `the President of the Supreme Court` EQUALS `paragraph 1, a judge`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose` EQUALS `paragraph 1, a judge`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `the Minister of Justice` EQUALS `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `the Knesset member of the coalition factions` EQUALS `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose` EQUALS `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `the Knesset member of the opposition factions` EQUALS `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose` EQUALS `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose`
-- A public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose is in none of the three: that is what s 4(d)(2), (3) say.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose` EQUALS `none of the three paragraphs`

§ `Counting`

#ASSERT `the number of members serving` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the number voting in favour` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 5

§ `The ordinary majority, s 4(d), no more than 80 coalition Knesset members`

-- all nine in favour
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- five: President, justice, Minister of Justice, coalition Knesset member, opposition Knesset member: one from each of (1), (2), (3)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- the opposition's public representative stands for paragraph (3)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- the coalition's public representative stands for paragraph (2): three judges, the opposition Knesset member and that representative
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- five without a judge: two ministers, the coalition Knesset member, the opposition Knesset member, the coalition's public representative
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- five without a member of paragraph (3)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- five without a member of paragraph (2)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- four, one from each paragraph and one more judge: not five
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `ordinary judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- a decision that is not the election of a judge takes the same majority
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `other decision` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `other decision` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `The Supreme Court majority, s 4(e), no more than 80 coalition Knesset members`

-- five with no judge: enough for the Supreme Court (the same five fail the ordinary majority above)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `supreme judge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- four in favour, one from each of (2) and (3): not five
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `supreme judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- the same four and the President: five, one from each of (2) and (3), the opposition's public representative standing for (3)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `supreme judge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- five judges and ministers with no member of paragraph (3)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `supreme judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- five with no member of paragraph (2)
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `supreme judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- four, with a judge, a minister, the coalition Knesset member and the opposition Knesset member: not five
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `supreme judge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `More than 80 coalition Knesset members, s 4(f)`

-- The nine under s 4(f), in order: President, justice, justice, Minister of Justice, other minister, coalition Knesset member, opposition Knesset member, two Knesset-chosen public representatives.
-- Supreme Court: five including two of the three (ministers and coalition Knesset member); no member of paragraph (3) and no judge needed.
-- Four in favour, two of the three: not five.
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine under section 4(f) in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `supreme judge` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine under section 4(f) in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `supreme judge` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- five in favour but only one of the three: a judge, a judge, the Minister of Justice and the two Knesset-chosen representatives
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine under section 4(f) in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `supreme judge` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- ordinary decision: five including a judge and two of the three
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine under section 4(f) in order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `ordinary judge` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- the same without a judge
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine under section 4(f) in order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `ordinary judge` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- the opposition Knesset member's consent is not needed (s 4(f)(3)): five without it, with a judge and two of the three (the Minister of Justice and the coalition Knesset member), pass
#ASSERT `the majority of section 4 is met` (`the nine under section 4(f) in order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `ordinary judge` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 4(f)(1): each of the three from a different faction`

#ASSERT `the composition meets section 4(f)(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the composition meets section 4(f)(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Below 80 the requirement does not arise.
#ASSERT `the composition meets section 4(f)(1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
